[{:db/id "q-343110/selection/eeeeebc3f49c3c9113412ed96e27bb6964f4a0cf996a6f01748457a954e2d578" :answer/id #uuid "d07c0b75-bb23-52b6-b96f-30d1a9a2e8bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343110/selection/b54d35f5cd27418fd414fe6cee9d4d1d97e5cd7243e49d4e4cee42282696792b" :answer/id #uuid "cae2b1cb-de48-5392-ae95-6dbb3e35566c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343110/selection/c1b9efac5a331db4fe8d16961a4e76e0fd8eb32c9f0b8cb13bcf76ee36a09ee5" :answer/id #uuid "4a3bd02a-ea68-50d4-be82-2b6a73294919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+12}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343110/selection/d0beb9d127c8cf703dd9d99602c2d6ac25d12176ca33148200a0bf321624609d" :answer/id #uuid "c4da58da-5cc5-5ced-81cf-3a41be481c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+8s+12}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343110/selection/15fe2e5fa42eebaf1a29793346c953f1d571530c2fcadaa5c988ee65863fef55" :answer/id #uuid "0c2bd063-1dbf-58df-afb5-388fe0385026" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+8s+15}{3s(s-1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343110/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c11fea9-f8dc-53c5-853b-3d0025d40343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-343110/selection/b54d35f5cd27418fd414fe6cee9d4d1d97e5cd7243e49d4e4cee42282696792b" :answer-field/choices ["q-343110/selection/eeeeebc3f49c3c9113412ed96e27bb6964f4a0cf996a6f01748457a954e2d578" "q-343110/selection/b54d35f5cd27418fd414fe6cee9d4d1d97e5cd7243e49d4e4cee42282696792b" "q-343110/selection/c1b9efac5a331db4fe8d16961a4e76e0fd8eb32c9f0b8cb13bcf76ee36a09ee5" "q-343110/selection/d0beb9d127c8cf703dd9d99602c2d6ac25d12176ca33148200a0bf321624609d" "q-343110/selection/15fe2e5fa42eebaf1a29793346c953f1d571530c2fcadaa5c988ee65863fef55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343110" :question/id #uuid "f1155af6-d35d-51d3-b6a5-6b676a893cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-343110" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>2$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=5-2{e}^{-t},\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{5-2{e}^{-t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =5L{1}-2L{{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0} \\\\ L{{e}^{at}} & =\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-(-1)}=\\frac{1}{s+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =5L{1}-2L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\ (sY(s)-\\frac{1}{3})-2Y(s) & =\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{2}{s+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s(s+1)+15(s+1)-6s}{3s(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+10s+15}{3s(s+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343110/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343110"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871/selection/4ac175a965815d044bb6e5ec17eeae075239c29a80070b3bca48326cdb71aece" :answer/id #uuid "5ce1e423-ed56-56b7-8e70-db0ba70db09a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871/selection/9941713cd30c3e4ce2cba532f19190106abe82e7725d9b970edc0f4adcf4bd89" :answer/id #uuid "01f868dd-ab7d-545c-9d3f-2aafc72bfe86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871/selection/c8ec1c70cefdcb68a61781313c2060fb587fb345a0d8a36c91ced37a2634bbf9" :answer/id #uuid "0b62bfad-3067-590d-b150-9cf0b4711145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871/selection/4129e16ae82f04f60958048044f1aecc5986d58936b4db74b6cf446b07a24613" :answer/id #uuid "cb5658fd-46fe-5fcb-99a4-8688e6af657a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871/selection/ae160808a7a157326e16a999a9ef19ad0a262e259828e3443b9cbb0d5e6a04c7" :answer/id #uuid "2777dd67-f9cf-594b-8bfb-ed1af76d7797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ac1d161-04fb-5d09-ba47-f01cbbfa805a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-342871/selection/ae160808a7a157326e16a999a9ef19ad0a262e259828e3443b9cbb0d5e6a04c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-342871/selection/4ac175a965815d044bb6e5ec17eeae075239c29a80070b3bca48326cdb71aece" "q-342871/selection/9941713cd30c3e4ce2cba532f19190106abe82e7725d9b970edc0f4adcf4bd89" "q-342871/selection/c8ec1c70cefdcb68a61781313c2060fb587fb345a0d8a36c91ced37a2634bbf9" "q-342871/selection/4129e16ae82f04f60958048044f1aecc5986d58936b4db74b6cf446b07a24613" "q-342871/selection/ae160808a7a157326e16a999a9ef19ad0a262e259828e3443b9cbb0d5e6a04c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342871" :question/id #uuid "8a59cf6b-30d9-5a4e-b2af-691e5237e06b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342871" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>2$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-2y=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)-2Y(s) & =-5(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ sY(s)-2Y(s) & =1-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>2,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-2)(s+2)}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-342871/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482/selection/eef045b8c8696e087b3f4e5dcc13d0b17c24884a9bd751f446749a9528fea496" :answer/id #uuid "4a536516-694a-58cf-bde1-43abb8d8d33a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{s(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482/selection/3de1ae628af3b119cd5bd95de07d15668ce882e1621c1dd346e5ef964cb9e94c" :answer/id #uuid "28957ba5-c113-5005-a547-95c52aab98bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{4s+1}{2{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482/selection/559cd4851647a8688f67d43413095a915dd2bd95f3220cf1f9637ee68b971293" :answer/id #uuid "080aad2f-0a38-52fa-9cc6-190d356821c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482/selection/4e0600ebc75939a60c991f9d931e9cc942f19833121da4e0a11c6febeb4d97ed" :answer/id #uuid "dcf00a22-6595-513b-a712-3b6539f99041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482/selection/b82e713a6e93a4395179362fe51c38681817330a5bc1513c648d1b31ea09e1c9" :answer/id #uuid "26b06a91-be56-5f1f-91c0-226da90a3878" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}+1}{4s(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d2df3f1-109f-5092-9d75-68ae8e81af3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64482/selection/559cd4851647a8688f67d43413095a915dd2bd95f3220cf1f9637ee68b971293" :answer-field/choices ["q-64482/selection/eef045b8c8696e087b3f4e5dcc13d0b17c24884a9bd751f446749a9528fea496" "q-64482/selection/3de1ae628af3b119cd5bd95de07d15668ce882e1621c1dd346e5ef964cb9e94c" "q-64482/selection/559cd4851647a8688f67d43413095a915dd2bd95f3220cf1f9637ee68b971293" "q-64482/selection/4e0600ebc75939a60c991f9d931e9cc942f19833121da4e0a11c6febeb4d97ed" "q-64482/selection/b82e713a6e93a4395179362fe51c38681817330a5bc1513c648d1b31ea09e1c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64482" :question/id #uuid "d18fffc1-68fb-5dfb-a521-2a4ffbf9bc9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-64482" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>0$ if\n\n$$\n2{y}^{′}+2y=4+{t}^{2},\\,y(0)=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{2{y}^{′}+2y} & =L{4+{t}^{2}} \\\\ 2L{{y}^{′}}+2L{y} & =4L{1}+L{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2L{{y}^{′}}+2L{y} & =4L{1}+L{{t}^{2}} \\\\ 2sY(s)+2Y(s) & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ (2s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2(2{s}^{2}+1)}{{s}^{3}(2s+2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64482/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64482"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473/selection/39c88ebd1e32f7426b85c104b5f22eefb0fe72f0462c6cbc254191553a5b9af7" :answer/id #uuid "d2f65c39-da30-50e6-9fa4-2eed0a90465a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473/selection/1bf55a84a6de8f6ff9858937206f262fd490f30d2fa978f0043effdbcea82bfa" :answer/id #uuid "b5e38a32-aa05-5f79-8892-51b357b4c656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473/selection/05aaeb73a62df7f2dccbb739545bb614bca5dc941ae1a57a086f0c38971350d7" :answer/id #uuid "b1ae5660-cc3b-51f5-aca8-bb968f9d26b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473/selection/2404e0507aac7628aa79aefd5a0e2c984efc68e901567bd595ee5220f116f33e" :answer/id #uuid "b59f2167-cb9b-50e0-995d-e1740cb41e6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473/selection/69552b8ad5958162371f6c673cddd0c9963254f7455408d85a83038b425045e0" :answer/id #uuid "546d319e-b90c-5d52-a99e-42e555a43a83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s+9}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5e86f9-4acc-50bb-a684-a4e69ad551c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-342473/selection/2404e0507aac7628aa79aefd5a0e2c984efc68e901567bd595ee5220f116f33e" :answer-field/choices ["q-342473/selection/39c88ebd1e32f7426b85c104b5f22eefb0fe72f0462c6cbc254191553a5b9af7" "q-342473/selection/1bf55a84a6de8f6ff9858937206f262fd490f30d2fa978f0043effdbcea82bfa" "q-342473/selection/05aaeb73a62df7f2dccbb739545bb614bca5dc941ae1a57a086f0c38971350d7" "q-342473/selection/2404e0507aac7628aa79aefd5a0e2c984efc68e901567bd595ee5220f116f33e" "q-342473/selection/69552b8ad5958162371f6c673cddd0c9963254f7455408d85a83038b425045e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342473" :question/id #uuid "68891c85-8075-57df-acec-5850a69663ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-342473" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>3$ if \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+y=-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>|\\omega |.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+y} & =L{-8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =-8L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9},\\,s>3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+L{y} & =-8L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)+Y(s) & =-8(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\ sY(s)+Y(s) & =1-\\frac{8s}{{s}^{2}-9} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-8s-9}{{s}^{2}-9} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-8s-9}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>3,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{({s}^{2}-8s-9)}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-9)(s+1)}{({s}^{2}-9)(s+1)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s-9}{{s}^{2}-9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-342473/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342473"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480/selection/bfc64b165ec77773ccf41a84bfddb756d36141930a7f6fe547dc673676a46b3b" :answer/id #uuid "90044f58-b7b7-522b-85ce-818154fcc86e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}+1}{s(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480/selection/1f6fe860e8bda7e2aba0880eca7f13d496b72ae716444736f896ab309cb65284" :answer/id #uuid "9a9fce76-5d04-56f9-b58b-5175843b85e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{s-3}{s+4},\\,s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480/selection/87c3a6c98a972f81c2d3fd2ba511c4d955c1818e6cbadda9fbbea6d2721c9028" :answer/id #uuid "17fd459e-9408-5baa-b98d-d135c26ab358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480/selection/1f91dfa604b80164c80415df897e390a4037e389201033065fc4bf8322ee682a" :answer/id #uuid "534be448-b414-51cd-a75e-f898be084991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{5{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{3}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480/selection/16314e66d8fcff8c0c39d4ca2a0455f2a3e2718b9777e954a12e62659d13f525" :answer/id #uuid "da631c34-f90b-51ac-916a-1e7ff25bfae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)},\\,s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "45c89ceb-0a77-5232-8f9f-727cb0c5e5b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64480/selection/87c3a6c98a972f81c2d3fd2ba511c4d955c1818e6cbadda9fbbea6d2721c9028" :answer-field/choices ["q-64480/selection/bfc64b165ec77773ccf41a84bfddb756d36141930a7f6fe547dc673676a46b3b" "q-64480/selection/1f6fe860e8bda7e2aba0880eca7f13d496b72ae716444736f896ab309cb65284" "q-64480/selection/87c3a6c98a972f81c2d3fd2ba511c4d955c1818e6cbadda9fbbea6d2721c9028" "q-64480/selection/1f91dfa604b80164c80415df897e390a4037e389201033065fc4bf8322ee682a" "q-64480/selection/16314e66d8fcff8c0c39d4ca2a0455f2a3e2718b9777e954a12e62659d13f525"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64480" :question/id #uuid "7d5c1cef-5ffa-52dc-89d4-1aa20679c3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-64480" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s)=L{y(t)}$ for $s>0$ if\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=2+t,\\,y(0)=3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}+4y} & =L{2+t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}+4L{y} & =2L{1}+L{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=3:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)=sY(s)-3\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s} \\\\ L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}+4L{y} & =2L{1}+L{t} \\\\ (sY(s)-3)+4Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ sY(s)+4Y(s) & =3+\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+4)Y(s) & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}+2s+1}{{s}^{2}(s+4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64480/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1417a42-f47a-5611-84be-f331c75287a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64480"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342499/field-1/6f974a3897bff64087eb39e9d5500ec295d32eeaa288315182dc96b28b1b6cf1" :answer/id #uuid "16cc6f65-d95e-51fc-8020-f6a8851828de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-3)(s+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342499/field-1/8011bcb76730cc575b53f75952e9df7f322da213216ae05010531c848ac2ec01" :answer/id #uuid "b5fad86a-f336-50f9-aa55-69c947778b25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{(s-3)(s+9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342499/field-1/6d4a956fc488dbbc52bd16a6dfd278d86f0767a9038d1495ec3a315bc8d6efc6" :answer/id #uuid "4d82507e-cfd4-5c70-8253-d38c28c3b66f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{(s-5)(s+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342499/field-1/fe1423dce08c05011bcb50982048c62b71a6cec9000f45d510dd4f90880b83d2" :answer/id #uuid "7080d319-d36f-5394-8eec-db1fe7d73ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-3)(s+9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342499/field-1/f8a66b75767a46f8f1203029b3b14147b1e62d396173b12373087c9e54bee44e" :answer/id #uuid "f0c76abd-2ff9-506d-a662-41eee89b0af1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s-9)(s+5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342499/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a51e059-6b87-5a34-aa48-c82b7b72c38c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answe