asoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},\\,s>0,\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+L{y}=2L{t}+4L{1}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard polynomial transforms\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1!}{{s}^{1+1}}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}, \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{0!}{{s}^{0+1}}=\\frac{1}{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+Y(s) & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ (s+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+1)$ and a repeated linear factor ${s}^{2},$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4s+2}{{s}^{2}(s+1)}=\\frac{A}{s}+\\frac{B}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4s+2=As(s+1)+B(s+1)+C{s}^{2}\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-1,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4(-1)+2=A(0)+B(0)+C(-1)^{2}\\,⟹\\,-2=C\\,⟹\\,C=-2.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=0,$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n4(0)+2=A(0)+B(0+1)+C(0)\\,⟹\\,2=B\\,⟹\\,B=2.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of $s,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4=A+B\\,⟹\\,4=A+2\\,⟹\\,A=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} & =1 \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}} & =t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}-2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\ y(t) & =2+2t-2{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342704/field-1" "q-342704/field-2" "q-342704/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eae6b5d-adff-53b2-970d-f0dcee58365f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342704"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342928/field-1/e24a52e37d3d61b1f6fced3f6f1f37727b7ba99f2a8983ed5bd326fec3c1e0b7" :answer/id #uuid "8f71dcbd-62b0-5322-9abc-cd2714975b33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(s+3)(s-2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342928/field-1/fab4939d7ba87978c46bbaffc743841e9b80c0ef3d305a065e021df81b94ff2d" :answer/id #uuid "bb6e7ff3-c99b-5237-b7c8-e95361ba1132" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s+8}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342928/field-1/02fe4f7ccdb00de77a7634a126d7bb4d99a9a58f2a0d2343e72f0e3238b77fac" :answer/id #uuid "a6017f00-685d-543b-b09e-60738602220e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342928/field-1/c6c29b7e5de254c820072279810fa747aa338c6b02b2197943f9e9f53bae4650" :answer/id #uuid "db7057ce-f702-51f2-b075-141dad40ffcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s+3)(s+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342928/field-1/ca368d9bdf9fc2f8ccc6fa8a8557b6926a880b70af3396629dea905156fd8d93" :answer/id #uuid "4ed51709-652b-5c4d-8441-c5657827