id #uuid "faf6eaf8-d467-5ca6-b6cc-ddf872d10da4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9466f2c-8e0d-55c6-92e8-36aeaddfcbc5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343063/field-2/537108ea870f1426f1dc8b1ebc958322bf808a2092c7c43eada0608755efad15" :answer-field/choices ["q-343063/field-2/537108ea870f1426f1dc8b1ebc958322bf808a2092c7c43eada0608755efad15" "q-343063/field-2/fab3f02b6eff2ee7a9f8cae1c16e9beb6888a7000ec0125ee8caf7637d675750" "q-343063/field-2/731acd74ad0fb39e2a2df12285f85480bcd2374ce765e8893b26410bda3fed07" "q-343063/field-2/adee1b793a2c3ade7d5c759219a236c7ad10122c18e236de5695f28f9ccd4eac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063/field-3/96876c1202c15f6f77453e0e3e8a3b003ba00347bb2720ec6b51d589012d746a" :answer/id #uuid "b52b8c1a-2149-5e3c-bddb-930baf24f1f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063/field-3/5fa0589a87ddb6c0f9756220ead3e9c5eb42c57d533a7a6c8366a30d5c124136" :answer/id #uuid "be2ac929-bdad-5d8d-9c2d-68dad3336e4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063/field-3/f5f85951d1e95c783eed9150f7c861860c5d9e9d234434622cf0735916cf6c0b" :answer/id #uuid "9e22ad16-56d2-5b2b-8d30-fb1f7f3284de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063/field-3/6f2af5b8d83f18216891fa4feaf2ba1f1bc70657c80fb54e068dfa9233f7360e" :answer/id #uuid "b004108b-23f4-5a63-b752-f4475b205710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b341a77-30d1-5a15-929c-9c7272dec395" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343063/field-3/5fa0589a87ddb6c0f9756220ead3e9c5eb42c57d533a7a6c8366a30d5c124136" :answer-field/choices ["q-343063/field-3/96876c1202c15f6f77453e0e3e8a3b003ba00347bb2720ec6b51d589012d746a" "q-343063/field-3/5fa0589a87ddb6c0f9756220ead3e9c5eb42c57d533a7a6c8366a30d5c124136" "q-343063/field-3/f5f85951d1e95c783eed9150f7c861860c5d9e9d234434622cf0735916cf6c0b" "q-343063/field-3/6f2af5b8d83f18216891fa4feaf2ba1f1bc70657c80fb54e068dfa9233f7360e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343063" :question/id #uuid "ba6ac491-3a92-5a80-bc18-d0291dfbd502" :question/math-academy-id "q-343063" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+3y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+3L{y}=2L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}-3L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-(-2))+3Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4})-3(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}) \\\\ (s+3)Y(s)+2 & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, subtract $2$ from the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-2 \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-3s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{2({s}^{2}+4)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ (s+3)Y(s) & =\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+3)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+4),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{s}^{2}-3s-4}{(s+3)({s}^{2}+4)}=\\frac{A}{s+3}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n-2{s}^{2}-3s-4=A({s}^{2}+4)+(Bs+C)(s+3)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-2(-3)^{2}-3(-3)-4=A((-3)^{2}+4)+0\\,⟹\\,-13=13A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n-2=A+B\\,⟹\\,-2=-1+B\\,⟹\\,B=-1.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n-4=4A+3C\\,⟹\\,-4=4(-1)+3C\\,⟹\\,C=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=-\\frac{1}{s+3}+\\frac{-s}{{s}^{2}+4}=-\\frac{1}{s+3}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =-{e}^{-3t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343063/field-1" "q-343063/field-2" "q-343063/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343063"] :db/ensure [:k