re [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b371c09-1b84-5c40-a240-3336bafbae33" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342962/field-2/40d4165ae3a3eabe715ede2d5477c1d21d1c2b652af499468fe5bbf1250d218a" :answer-field/choices ["q-342962/field-2/3cc060f6f1eed6365ea54b8d0fba63ece3cafaae9cef82cbd2482381ee1ed4fe" "q-342962/field-2/40d4165ae3a3eabe715ede2d5477c1d21d1c2b652af499468fe5bbf1250d218a" "q-342962/field-2/f27b351728b8d29cef550bceca29677af3c80750d9ebae136e7c25b95e506920" "q-342962/field-2/7c0a1d9b8cf86f5879d4da631479bde8e7c4cfef06f1575a0ec7deeafb2449fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962/field-3/d543112fbe074ef133deed170cc6053c14cf1486daa3f7ed04014d25275b92db" :answer/id #uuid "4501155a-4863-57de-a6c0-fb1a9373e798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-6t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962/field-3/d0acdc4b70c4d12ea6815c8e317977edb9ca94492449679886fc9d8a36db8d6c" :answer/id #uuid "1e424a2b-53c7-50b4-a3a6-d51b4a1381ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}+\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962/field-3/cf6a7be7c180f2591e10eefd718e79fbfc4d24f34a527226d5745587d3c6aeeb" :answer/id #uuid "ca5e7db2-5f33-5442-b570-67b23362de91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}-\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962/field-3/3b530e60534ca8dedd38eb271a181197c1d2628b9a025125159de549d48407e2" :answer/id #uuid "d10e5897-d51d-5566-a824-444b8fb7a7a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}-\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "435efd9b-b860-5744-8489-57d886c5daa0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342962/field-3/d0acdc4b70c4d12ea6815c8e317977edb9ca94492449679886fc9d8a36db8d6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342962/field-3/d543112fbe074ef133deed170cc6053c14cf1486daa3f7ed04014d25275b92db" "q-342962/field-3/d0acdc4b70c4d12ea6815c8e317977edb9ca94492449679886fc9d8a36db8d6c" "q-342962/field-3/cf6a7be7c180f2591e10eefd718e79fbfc4d24f34a527226d5745587d3c6aeeb" "q-342962/field-3/3b530e60534ca8dedd38eb271a181197c1d2628b9a025125159de549d48407e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342962" :question/id #uuid "fe117573-5606-5478-b552-48739b413505" :question/math-academy-id "q-342962" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+6y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+6L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}+L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}=\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+6Y(s) & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}+\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\ (s+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+3}{{s}^{2}+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+6),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+6)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+9),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{s+3}{(s+6)({s}^{2}+9)}=\\frac{A}{s+6}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+9}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\ns+3=A({s}^{2}+9)+(Bs+C)(s+6)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-6,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n-6+3=A((-6)^{2}+9)+0\\,⟹\\,-3=45A\\,⟹\\,A=-\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=-\\frac{1}{15}+B\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n3=9A+6C\\,⟹\\,3=-\\frac{3}{5}+6C\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{15})}{s+6}+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{15}s+\\frac{3}{5})}{{s}^{2}+9}=-\\frac{1}{15(s+6)}+\\frac{s+9}{15({s}^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+6}} & ={e}^{-6t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{15}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+6}}+\\frac{1}{15}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}}+\\frac{1}{5}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}} \\\\ y(t) & =-\\frac{1}{15}{e}^{-6t}+\\frac{1}{15}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342962/field-1" "q-342962/field-2" "q-342962/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342962"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/v