ac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342960/field-3/8107e1c106c16f2e570a94a772b8c51e7af8e0921535d41fefe5573bd28b5164" :answer/id #uuid "66fd85df-5d7d-5477-ae5f-1711c169e460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342960/field-3/da69f6fc321ab8e55c0ff47bac9d6436b4f9dcde9ceb50125511f55d63f23a67" :answer/id #uuid "63030385-ff8e-51e6-a1cb-fe62adcd0514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342960/field-3/b2fdaf7b640eeed7ec2ee5c6dc21256b11077f9b1794dcee485d96849bf666f0" :answer/id #uuid "f3d2e46e-dbf3-5db8-a56b-cff411b52180" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342960/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "274d1f01-5a5a-556d-ae0c-af145b61fc53" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342960/field-3/bbc9e0eff49f5e9166fcbf1900badee679ba0b99142f5869453634d381c5b37a" :answer-field/choices ["q-342960/field-3/bbc9e0eff49f5e9166fcbf1900badee679ba0b99142f5869453634d381c5b37a" "q-342960/field-3/8107e1c106c16f2e570a94a772b8c51e7af8e0921535d41fefe5573bd28b5164" "q-342960/field-3/da69f6fc321ab8e55c0ff47bac9d6436b4f9dcde9ceb50125511f55d63f23a67" "q-342960/field-3/b2fdaf7b640eeed7ec2ee5c6dc21256b11077f9b1794dcee485d96849bf666f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342960" :question/id #uuid "1873e66d-b721-525d-8ac0-7b13c3d92c58" :question/math-academy-id "q-342960" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+2y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+2L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}-L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+2Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-s}{{s}^{2}+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+2)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+16),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}=\\frac{A}{s+2}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+16}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4-s=A({s}^{2}+16)+(Bs+C)(s+2)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4-(-2)=A((-2)^{2}+16)+0\\,⟹\\,6=20A\\,⟹\\,A=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=\\frac{3}{10}+B\\,⟹\\,B=-\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n4=16A+2C\\,⟹\\,4=\\frac{48}{10}+2C\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}+\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{10}s-\\frac{2}{5})}{{s}^{2}+16}=\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\frac{3}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}-\\frac{3}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}}-\\frac{1}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342960/field-1" "q-342960/field-2" "q-342960/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342960"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342961/field-1/55c082dc131abec153f8eee59abe326cb472acfab5fb0b7e8425992478d7d8cf" :answer/id #uuid "fbd6831c-9723-5189-8d55-ec7ddaa56480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342961/field-1/f67762574637e0997f0f2093a0b5fa05650b82f58b2d384414dcab1fb454166b" :answer/id #uuid "9526f984-319a-5b30-b137-df0bc184474d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s-1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342961/field-1/04c99863504b34aabe92d131901ae1bcd28d1985e7504f42e4eb32d43f119229" :answer/id #uuid "7da514e5-20be-57aa-8353-8795fb167de3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s+1}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342961/field-1/fcfde82e3d17d5250cf8fdd5f03ca9c96a9b63916825ee057640b5395e639ad4" :answer/id #uuid "9041cf93-3